! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 4 (0:28-0:40): Redox control -- temperature sweep
! =============================================================================
! Same midpoint salt as 03_redox_UF35.ti (F=135.5, U(IV)/U(III) ~ 1), swept
! 800-1400 K in 50 K steps to show the redox ratio is nearly temperature
! independent. `reinit` warm-starts each point from the previous solution
! (big speedup on a sweep); `heat capacity` also reports Cp/H/S.
!
! This writes JSON to outputs/salt_training_sweep -- feed it to
! doc/training/make_figures.py for the U(IV)/U(III) figure.
!
! IMPORTANT JSON gotcha (verified): the MSFL phase block has NO "species" key.
! It uses "cations"/"anions"/"quadruplets" (MQMQA/SUBQ format). Cation names
! are truncated to 8 characters -- U(IV) constituents appear as "U[CN=VI]",
! "U[CN=VII" (truncated), and "U[Dimer]" (counts double, it's a U2 dimer).
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/03_redox_sweep.ti
! Verified: 13 points, ~4.8 s wall time, U(IV)/U(III) = 1.000 at every T.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 800:1400:50
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 66.0       ! Li
mass(4)           = 33.0       ! Be
mass(92)          = 1.0        ! U
mass(9)           = 135.5      ! F
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 1
write json        = .TRUE.
output            = salt_training_sweep
reinit            = .TRUE.
heat capacity     = .TRUE.
